# Keeps the Docker build context small. All three services in
# docker/docker-compose.yml build with `context: ..` -- the repo root -- so
# without this file every `docker compose build` hands the daemon the entire
# checkout. On a full development clone that is ~22GB, the bulk of it the
# Android SDL3 submodules, sanitizer/wasm build trees and git history, none of
# which any Dockerfile copies. It is paid per build, and the site image is now
# rebuilt on every content change (see docker/Dockerfile.site), so it stopped
# being merely wasteful.
#
# Deliberately a denylist of the known-large, known-unneeded paths rather than
# an allowlist (`*` plus `!` re-includes): a future Dockerfile that copies
# something new keeps working, instead of failing on a missing file that is
# silently absent from the context. Between the three Dockerfiles the context
# needs only server/, CMakeLists.txt, site/, tools/build-site.py and
# docs/{PRIVACY_POLICY.md,screenshots,store-assets} -- all left in.

# Android port: SDL3/SDL3_image/SDL3_mixer submodules, Gradle caches. 15GB.
android/

# Git history. Nothing is built from it -- the fb-server image compiles from
# the copied sources, not from a checkout.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Local build trees, including the sanitizer and wasm ones.
build/
build-*/
dist-wasm/
cmake-build-*/

# Worktrees are full copies of the repo, so they would otherwise be sent
# alongside it.
.worktrees/
.claude/

# Editor/OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Never belongs in an image, and docker/ssl holds real certificate material
# on a deployed host. nginx.conf and the certs reach the container as
# bind mounts declared in docker-compose.yml, not through the build context.
docker/ssl/
docker/.env
docker/push-credentials/
